<a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/jon-prosser/">Jon Prosser</a> is arguing that Apple's alleged trade secrets are now public, while the company seeks his YouTube revenue records, channel analytics, and third-party messages to investigate his alleged financial gain from leaks about <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ios-26/">iOS 26</a>.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2025/10/Jon-Prosser-Rainbow.jpg" alt="" width="1600" height="900" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1022982" /><br/>
In a new <a href="https://www.courtlistener.com/docket/70833801/38/apple-inc-v-ramacciotti/">joint status report filed yesterday</a>, Apple said it is still waiting for YouTube revenue reports, channel analytics, and third-party communications requested from Prosser more than three months ago. The materials concern his alleged financial gain and how Apple's confidential information was obtained and shared, continuing the discovery dispute <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/08/07/apple-flags-delays-in-its-prosser-lawsuit/">detailed in August</a>.<br/>
<br/>
Prosser's lawyer says he has already fulfilled the discovery obligations agreed to when the parties <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/06/11/apple-agrees-to-let-jon-prosser-contest-lawsuit/">sought to set aside</a> the default against him. He says Apple keeps requesting more documents each time records are produced.<br/>
<br/>
His attorney also argues that Apple's identified trade secrets are now public following the release of &zwnj;iOS 26&zwnj; and macOS 26, and questions whether some were ever secret given earlier third-party disclosures. He says Apple's written descriptions lack corresponding images, making its claims difficult to assess.<br/>
<br/>
Apple disputes that its disclosure is deficient and says it is willing to discuss it with the defendants' lawyers. It also says Prosser's deposition testimony and his Signal exchanges with Michael Ramacciotti suggest the pair coordinated to obtain and disclose confidential information for financial gain, contradicting Ramacciotti's denial of a conspiracy.<br/>
<br/>
Ramacciotti wants to distance his case from Prosser's defense, with his lawyer saying he is "unwilling to be drawn into it." He has asked Judge James Donato for an October conference at which Apple would explain what further evidence it needs, followed by a deadline within 30 days to dismiss its claims against him or commit to trial. He now conditions a second deposition and updated written answers on Apple first providing a roadmap to resolution.<br/>
<br/>
Apple <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2025/07/17/apple-sues-jon-prosser-ios-26-leaks/">filed the lawsuit in July 2025</a>, alleging that Prosser and Ramacciotti coordinated to access an Apple employee's development iPhone and profit from unreleased software information. Prosser published videos showing recreations of &zwnj;iOS 26&zwnj;'s Liquid Glass redesign before Apple's announcement. Apple is seeking damages and an injunction against further disclosure of its trade secrets.<br/>
<br/>
In his <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/07/02/jon-prosser-responds-to-apple-leaks-lawsuit/">July 2 response to the lawsuit</a>, Prosser admitted participating in a <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/facetime/">FaceTime</a> call during which Ramacciotti showed him features running on the development device. He denied participating in a coordinated scheme or that the information he viewed constituted trade secrets.<br/>
<br/>
